# These notebooks are packaged verbatim into the handoff zip, and that zip's
# sha256 is quoted as its identity.
#
# make_operator_notebooks.py writes them with LF. Left to its default, git would
# check them out as CRLF on Windows, the packager would zip those bytes, and the
# package would hash differently on a fresh clone than it does here -- the same
# class of defect the packager's own ZIP_EPOCH comment exists to prevent, arriving
# by a different route. -text stops git touching the bytes.
*.ipynb -text
